From 09ed652ccc53ab23c73434491ecd4dd1420d9e22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:37:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/32] Skip HTML interchange and style markup inside foreign
 content on copy

Prevent StyledMarkupSerializer and StyledMarkupAccumulator from emitting
HTML interchange markup (<span>&nbsp;</span> and
<br class="Apple-interchange-newline">) or inline style wrappers
(<span style="...">) inside foreign content such as <math> and <svg>.

When the HTML parser parses a serialized <math> or <svg> fragment,
encountering <span> or <br> inside a non-integration-point foreign
element triggers a foreign-content breakout that pops <math> or <svg>
off the open element stack and parses subsequent siblings in the HTML
namespace.

Specifically:
- Add IsInForeignContentForSerialization() to detect when a node or any
  of its DOM or flat-tree ancestors is a non-HTML element or has a
  "math" or "svg" tag name.
- Skip inline style <span> wrapping and
  ConvertHtmlTextToInterchangeFormat() in
  StyledMarkupAccumulator::AppendTextWithInlineStyle() and
  StyledMarkupTraverser::ShouldApplyWrappingStyle() when inside foreign
  content.
- Avoid emitting leading or trailing interchange newlines inside foreign
  content in StyledMarkupSerializer::CreateMarkup(), and advance
  first_node to the highest <math> ancestor when a leading interchange
  newline precedes a <math> subtree.
- Do not abort the ancestor wrapping loop in CreateMarkup() when
  traversing block or table ancestors (such as <mtd> or <mtr>) inside a
  <math> ancestor that must be serialized.

Guard the behavior behind the SkipHtmlInterchangeInForeignContent
runtime enabled feature.

